config DRM_PARHELIA
	tristate "Matrox Parhelia"
	depends on DRM && PCI
	select DRM_GEM_VRAM_HELPER
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select I2C
	select I2C_ALGOBIT
	select FW_LOADER
	select CRC32
	help
	  DRM driver for the Matrox Parhelia P-series (Parhelia-512, Parhelia8x,
	  Parhelia-LX and P690) graphics adapters.  It provides native KMS for
	  the primary display controller, VRAM GEM objects and a validated DMA
	  submission interface for the WARP 3D engine.

	  Requires the locally extracted parhelia/mtx*.bin resident firmware
	  files in /lib/firmware (also in the initramfs for early loading).

	  If compiled as a module, it will be called parhelia.

config DRM_M9X
	tristate "Matrox M9/Phoenix clean-room render driver"
	depends on DRM && PCI
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	help
	  Independent, render-only clean-room bring-up driver for Matrox
	  M9/Phoenix device 102b:0540.  It has no dependency on the Parhelia
	  P-series module and provides no display support yet.

	  m9_enable=1 is required before the driver binds.  It exposes DMA32 GEM
	  and a validate-only command interface.  m9_render_diag=1 is additionally
	  required for the kernel-owned writeback-fence diagnostic.

	  If compiled as a module, it will be called m9x_drm.
